From f0b485c9bcde6d1ae82134e9bae6dbbcaf182c88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:16:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 84/90] particle: the operators and initializers of WE's stock
 presets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 20 types only the stock presets use were dropped by the parser. Now (decoded from
wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485: the operator interpreter GH 0x140265800, jump table 0x140271798, the
parser GH 0x1401f3120's stores, its default functions GH 0x1401e7040…0x1401ee010):

- capvelocity (case 0x12): v ×= min (1, maxspeed / |v|), maxspeed × the speed override.
- maintaindistancetocontrolpoint (0xb): the particles move with the control point, then
  p = cp + (p − cp)(1 + k (distance / |p − cp| − 1)), k = 1 or clamp (variablestrength · dt).
- maintaindistancebetweencontrolpoints (0xc): the segment carries its particles when its ends
  move (the last step's segment → this step's, clamped t).
- reducemovementnearcontrolpoint (0xd): v ×= 1 − clamp (lerp (reductions, t) · dt).
- collisionbox: its jump-table entry is the next-operator label — a no-op in WE too.
- boids (0x11): every s-th particle per step (s = n / 200 + 1), factors × s; the forces are
  Reynolds' rules (inferred).
- remapvalue / remapinitialvalue: WE's enums (operation, the 20 values, components,
  transform functions) and defaults; the function shapes are inferred.
- collisionplane / sphere / quad / bounds: bounce (v −= (1 + b)(v · n) n), slide or delete
  (GH 0x1401edab0); geometry from the keys, partly inferred. collisionmodel is parsed and
  reported (it needs a model's triangles).
- inheritvaluefromevent / inheritinitialvaluefromevent: GH 0x140287030's table from the event
  particle (event children now keep it; a follow child's every step).
- hsvcolorrandom, colorlist, positionoffsetrandom, inheritcontrolpointvelocity (the control
  points' velocities are tracked), mapsequencebetweencontrolpoints: WE's keys and defaults,
  their runtime inferred where noted in CParticleStock.cpp.

A key's 3D or pixel default follows the scene's projection (inferred: the parser's flag).
The layerimage emitter is not done (it needs the layer's pixels on the CPU).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F6 (the stock-only particle operators)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
